---
description: Prevent false positives in harness self-tests.
alwaysApply: true
---

When executing harness/self-test checks:
1) Use direct exact-path reads as primary existence evidence.
2) Treat successful read as definitive existence.
3) Never mark missing based only on search output.
4) Require two failed checks before "missing".
5) If evidence conflicts, report "inconclusive" and include both observations.
